## Findings

### Was **Meir Shreibman** elected?

**The available evidence does not establish that Meir Shreibman was elected to the Sokółka community council.**

The Yizkor Book says that, shortly before the election, the **Non-Aligned Workers’ Party** appeared as an opponent of the Bund. Its list was headed by **Meyer Yulewitz and Meyer Schreiberman**. It also records that the two men spoke at a meeting in the old synagogue, urging voters to support list number 10. ([jewishgen.org](https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/sokolka/sok123.html?utm_source=openai))

However, the passage does **not** provide:

- the full slate of elected council members;
- the number of seats won by the Non-Aligned Workers’ Party;
- confirmation that either Yulewitz or Schreiberman entered the council;
- a later political role for Shreibman.

Therefore, Meir should currently be described as a **leader or head of the Non-Aligned Workers’ Party list and a campaign speaker**, not as a confirmed council member. The existing graph record titled “Election War for the Sokolka Community Council” should not be used as evidence that he was elected.

### Who was **Meyer Yulewitz**?

The Yizkor Book identifies **Meyer Yulewitz** as Meir Shreibman’s **political associate and co-head of the Non-Aligned Workers’ Party list**. Yulewitz and “Meyer Schreiberman” jointly addressed the workers’ meeting in the old synagogue on behalf of list number 10. ([jewishgen.org](https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/sokolka/sok123.html?utm_source=openai))

The available Sokółka material does not give Yulewitz’s:

- biography or occupation;
- family connections;
- dates of birth or death;
- later political career;
- election result or confirmed council membership.

The name **“Meyer Schreiberman”** is probably a variant or translation of **Meir Shreibman**, since the same passage identifies a Meyer Schreiberman as the second head of the list and speaker alongside Meyer Yulewitz. But the source does not explicitly equate the two names. That identification should therefore remain recorded as probable rather than certain.

### Recommended archival wording

> **Meir Shreibman**, also possibly recorded as **Meyer Schreiberman**, was a leader of the Non-Aligned Workers’ Party in Sokółka and co-head of its list with **Meyer Yulewitz** during the community-council election campaign. He spoke with Yulewitz at a meeting in the old synagogue in support of list number 10. The available source does not establish whether Shreibman or Yulewitz was elected to the council.
